  "transcript": [
    {
      "assistant": "Before midnight you told me the last of the guests had gone from Dad's seventieth. You'd washed about forty glasses and you were sitting in the kitchen next to an empty cake stand.\n\nThen it went past twelve. Callum stayed behind with the end of the port and the two of you dragged chairs out onto the patio, and that's when he told you about the job in Aberdeen. You said you weren't ready for how much it stung. After that he went up to bed and you stacked the folding chairs in the hall, slowly, one at a time. You found a last sausage roll under the foil and ate it cold, standing over the bin. You were wondering who'd do Sunday lunch with Dad once Callum has moved. And the clocks went back, so the cooker handed you quarter past one a second time.\n\nThat was all one night, Saturday into Sunday.",
      "at": "2026-10-26T12:00:00.000Z",
      "stepId": "night",
      "terminalEvent": "assistant_committed",
      "type": "say",
      "user": "What did I tell you on Saturday night before midnight, and what came once it was past midnight?"
    },
    {
      "assistant": "The sausage roll came first. You found it under the foil, ate it cold standing over the bin, and after that you were still up wondering about Sunday lunch with Dad — then you noticed the clocks had gone back.",
      "at": "2026-10-26T12:02:00.000Z",
      "stepId": "order",
      "terminalEvent": "assistant_committed",
      "type": "say",
      "user": "Which did I mention first, the last sausage roll or the clocks going back?"
